id: hr
name: Human resources and workforce
industry: Human resources
domain: Workforce management: organisation, positions, employees, recruitment, performance, learning, leave and pay
scope: Organisation units, jobs and positions, employees and their assignments, recruitment from requisition to offer, skills, performance reviews, learning, leave and attendance, compensation and payroll results.
summary: Describes an organisation's workforce: its structure and positions, the people who fill them, how they were hired, what they can do, how they perform and what they are paid. A starter model aligned to the W3C Organization ontology and the ESCO skills classification.
purpose: Shared vocabulary across HRIS, recruiting, learning and payroll systems; basis for headcount, attrition and skills analytics.
read: An Organisation unit contains Positions for a Job at a Grade and Work location. An Employee holds positions through Assignments and reports to a manager. Recruitment runs from a Job requisition through Applications by Candidates to an Offer. Employees have Skills, Performance reviews, Training enrolments, Leave requests and Compensation; Payslips record what was paid.
in: Organisation and positions; Employees and assignments; Recruitment; Skills, performance, learning; Leave; Compensation and payroll
out: Statutory filings detail; Benefits provider integrations; Time-clock hardware; Finance postings
std: org | high | Units, posts, roles and membership follow the W3C Organization Ontology. | org:OrganizationalUnit, org:Post, org:Role, org:Membership, org:Site
std: esco | medium | Occupations and skills are classified with ESCO. | esco:Occupation, esco:Skill
std: hrxml | medium | Candidate, position opening and payroll structures follow HR Open Standards. | Candidate, PositionOpening, PayrollInstruction
std: schema | low | People are aligned to schema.org. | schema:Person
== Structure | Organisation and positions | How the organisation is built.
OrganisationUnit | A division, department or team; units nest. | =org:OrganizationalUnit
  - unit code : string !
  - name : string !
  > part of > OrganisationUnit ?
  > headed by > Employee ?
Job | A kind of work with defined responsibilities, independent of who does it. | ~esco:Occupation
  - job code : string !
  - title : string !
  - job family : string
Grade | A level in the pay and seniority structure.
  - grade code : string !
  - minimum pay : decimal
  - maximum pay : decimal
WorkLocation | A site where people work. | ~org:Site
  - name : string !
  - city : string
  - country : string
Position | A specific seat in the organisation that one person can fill. | ~org:Post
  - position number : string !
  - approved from : date
  - vacant : boolean
  > in unit > OrganisationUnit 1
  > for job > Job 1
  > at grade > Grade ?
  > based at > WorkLocation ?
== People | Employees | Who works here.
Employee | A person employed by the organisation. | ~schema:Person
  - employee number : string !
  - name : string !
  - date of birth : date
  - gender : string
  - joined on : date !
  - left on : date
  > reports to > Employee ? | The employee's manager. | manages
  > has employment type > EmploymentType 1
  > has status > EmploymentStatus 1
EmploymentType | The contractual basis.
  * Permanent, Fixed term, Contractor, Intern, Part time
EmploymentStatus | Whether the person is currently employed.
  * Active, On leave, Notice period, Separated
Assignment | The placement of an employee in a position for a period.
  - start date : date !
  - end date : date
  - primary : boolean
  > of employee > Employee 1 | | has assignment
  > to position > Position 1
Separation | The end of an employment.
  - last working day : date !
  - voluntary : boolean
  > of employee > Employee 1
  > for reason > SeparationReason 1
SeparationReason | Why the person left.
  * Resignation, Retirement, End of contract, Termination, Redundancy
== Hiring | Recruitment | Bringing people in.
JobRequisition | An approved request to hire for a position.
  - requisition number : string !
  - opened on : date !
  - closed on : date
  > for position > Position 1
  > hiring manager > Employee 1
Candidate | A person being considered for employment.
  - name : string !
  - email : string
  - source : string
JobApplication | A candidate's application to a requisition.
  - applied on : date !
  > by candidate > Candidate 1
  > to requisition > JobRequisition 1 | | receives application
  > at stage > ApplicationStage 1
ApplicationStage | How far an application has progressed.
  * Applied, Screened, Interviewed, Offered, Hired, Rejected, Withdrawn
Interview | An assessment conversation with a candidate.
  - held on : dateTime !
  - rating : decimal
  - feedback : string
  > for application > JobApplication 1
  > conducted by > Employee +
Offer | A proposal of employment made to a candidate.
  - offered on : date !
  - offered pay : decimal
  - accepted : boolean
  > for application > JobApplication 1
== Growth | Skills, performance and learning | What people can do and how they develop.
Skill | An ability or area of knowledge. | ~esco:Skill
  - skill name : string !
  - category : string
EmployeeSkill | An employee's level in a skill.
  - proficiency level : integer !
  - assessed on : date
  > of employee > Employee 1
  > in skill > Skill 1
PerformanceReview | A periodic assessment of an employee.
  - period : string !
  - rating : decimal
  - comments : string
  > of employee > Employee 1
  > reviewed by > Employee 1
Course | A training offering.
  - course code : string !
  - title : string !
  - hours : decimal
  > develops > Skill *
TrainingEnrolment | An employee's participation in a course.
  - enrolled on : date
  - completed on : date
  - score : decimal
  > of employee > Employee 1
  > in course > Course 1
== Reward | Leave and pay | Time off and money.
LeaveRequest | A request for time off.
  - from date : date !
  - to date : date !
  - days : decimal
  - approved : boolean
  > by employee > Employee 1
  > of type > LeaveType 1
LeaveType | The kind of leave.
  * Annual, Sick, Maternity, Paternity, Unpaid, Compensatory
Compensation | An employee's agreed pay from a date.
  - effective from : date !
  - annual base pay : decimal !
  - variable pay percent : decimal
  - currency : string
  > of employee > Employee 1
Payslip | What an employee was paid for a period.
  - pay period : string !
  - gross pay : decimal !
  - deductions : decimal
  - net pay : decimal !
  > of employee > Employee 1
rule: constraint | One primary assignment | An active employee has exactly one primary assignment at a time. | Assignment, Employee
rule: constraint | Pay within grade | Annual base pay should lie between the minimum and maximum pay of the position's grade. | Compensation, Grade
rule: derivation | Attrition rate | Attrition is separations in a period divided by average active headcount. | Separation, Employee
rule: derivation | Time to hire | Time to hire is the days from requisition opening to offer acceptance. | JobRequisition, Offer
uc: Attrition by unit and reason | HR business partner | What is voluntary attrition by organisation unit and separation reason? | Separation, SeparationReason, Employee, Assignment, Position, OrganisationUnit | Separation.of employee, for reason, has assignment, to position, in unit, Separation.voluntary
uc: Open positions and time to hire | Talent acquisition lead | Which requisitions have been open longest, and what is average time to hire by job? | JobRequisition, Position, Job, JobApplication, Offer | for position, for job, receives application, Offer.for application, JobRequisition.opened on, Offer.offered on
uc: Skill gaps | Learning manager | Which skills required for a job family are below level 3 among its employees? | EmployeeSkill, Skill, Employee, Assignment, Position, Job | EmployeeSkill.of employee, in skill, EmployeeSkill.proficiency level, has assignment, to position, for job
